# Vercel uploads everything the function might need; `includeFiles` in
# vercel.json narrows the bundle to `dist/`, `static/`, `openapi.json` and
# `about.md`. Everything listed here exists only to build, test or operate the
# project elsewhere.
#
# `about.md` is deliberately *not* listed: it is seeded into the store at boot.
# (A `*.md` ignore with a `!about.md` negation does not work — Vercel keeps the
# first pattern that matches.)
.git
.github
.commandcode
docs
test
netlify
data
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.override.yml
Procfile
eslint.config.js
tsconfig.eslint.json
release-please-config.json
.release-please-manifest.json
